First of all, that's Sporkhack :) Sooo... arguably, Derek is succeeding
at making the late game harder, and making it much more challenging to
ascend with the stats someone would be able to "cakewalk" vanilla with.

I base this assertion on:

"Not by Demogoron (was wearing an AoLS when he got me), though an arch-
lich decided to invite Yeenoghu and Demogorgon over for a family get-
together. Not by Rodney, who showed up approximately ten times (was
wearing several different AoLS). The nasties simply waged a war of
attrition. Thus my Sporkhack high score simply reads: killed by a
stalker."

(If you still don't believe me, there's currently
http://nethack.nineball.org/dumps/Loser.lastlog which will soon go away
and I've "kindly" archived at http://autumnfox.akrasiac.org/Loser.lastlog
at least for the duration of this conversation. :) 

But even given that --- with all due respect to 3cnfsat, I also don't
think that he used all of the tactics available at his disposal, though
it still sounds like he got a tough endgame.

First, burning two amulets of lifesaving on Demogorgon means he was not
prepared; a character with two amulets of lifesaving surely could have
conjured up a scroll of scare monster. Yes, the Elbereth nerf means that
your old friends wand of fire and Magicbane can't carry you protected
through the dungeon like a pair of angel wings; no, it doesn't mean that
you can't still get 100% protection from something, it's just a war of
attrition when each scare monster burns either a scroll or a potion of
holy water.

Second, wearing even a +5 ring of increase damage over  a ring of
conflict when summon nasties is in play doesn't seem optimal to me;
3cnfsat can comment if he cares to about whether  or not he was using it
most of the time, but given his charisma (yes, given his charisma! I'm
glad Derek chose to implement my idea on that one) it would have been
effective had he done so.

Third, a priest is not a combat wombat. A priest needs to be run like a 
hybrid of a caster and a melee character. Even a tip-top Grayswandir with 
increase damage isn't going to compare to #twoweapon. If you really want
to bash things, play a valk or samurai or something.

Finally, it was a genoless game --- a challenge, conduct ascension. 
Genoless has plenty of teeth in vanilla, and I think this is ample
evidence that it has even more in Sporkhack. 

> So, quite possibly, the SporkHack agenda is
> fairly misguided, and instead attention to
> nerfing the worst of naked AC buildup means,
> alchemy overuse, polypiling, and other ways
> *deliberately* to _become_ a walking tank
> should be the focus.

It might still be misguided, but I don't think it's for the reasons you
think it is. If it is misguided, I'm guessing it's because it's forcing
players to burn resources but not the resources that matter. Here though
I think it was successful; 3cnfsat spent his resources to get amulets
of lifesaving and wands of teleportation and, while they were helpful,
they didn't take him all the way to the top. Perhaps sporkhack is not as
solved a resource collection problem as vanilla! Or, perhaps it will be
solved by some ingenious player who finds a hole in the balance system,
which will then be corrected! Luckily, it's under active and rapid
development for the moment, so Derek has the opportunity to respond to
these kind of issues if and when they come up. 

And if it's terribly misguided after all and everyone playing magically
stops having fun, well, we can all go back to waiting for 3.NEXT. :)

